{"id": "section-body-11095", "title": "Eclampsia", "chapterId": "chapter-eleven", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "OBSTETRICS, GYNECOLOGY AND CONTRACEPTION", "Antenatal Care", "Eclampsia"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-11095", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Eclampsia", "runs": [{"text": "Eclampsia"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1452"}}, {"id": "body-11096", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Eclampsia is a condition peculiar to pregnancy and post-partum periods, characterized by elevated BP and tonic-clonic convulsions which are not caused by epilepsy, severe malaria, meningitis, hypoglycemia or other causes of convulsions. Majority (50%) occur preterm. Eclampsia may occur without prior elevation of BP.", "runs": [{"text": "Eclampsia is a condition peculiar to pregnancy and post-partum periods, characterized by elevated BP and tonic-clonic convulsions which are not caused by epilepsy, severe malaria, meningitis, hypoglycemia or other causes of convulsions. Majority (50%) occur preterm. Eclampsia may occur without prior elevation of BP."}]}, {"id": "body-11097", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Diagnostic Criteria", "runs": [{"text": "Diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Criteria"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11098", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Signs of severe pre-eclampsia (BP >160/110mm Hg)", "runs": [{"text": "Signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pre-eclampsia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(BP"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">160/110mm"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hg)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1430"}}, {"id": "body-11099", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Loss of consciousness", "runs": [{"text": "Loss"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "consciousness"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1430"}}, {"id": "b